---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { proof } from "../data/services";
---

<Layout
  title="About | 17th Street Labs"
  description="Meet the founders and operating principles behind 17th Street Labs, an independent AI engineering and security research firm in Denver."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Experience without the institution.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        17th Street Labs is a founder-led AI engineering and security research
        firm. Small by design, direct by default, and built for work where
        judgment matters more than headcount.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <dl class="proof-strip">
        {proof.map(({ value, label }) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{value}</dt>
            <dd>{label}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="container section-grid">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2>Founders</h2>
        <p>Two people, one firm. You get both on every engagement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="founder-pair founder-pair-long">
        <article class="founder">
          <h3>Marina Levy</h3>
          <p class="role">Co-founder, chief executive officer</p>
          <p>
            Marina sets the operating direction for 17th Street Labs. She
            shapes ambitious technical work into focused engagements with a
            clear scope, a steady cadence, and an outcome we can be held to.
            If an engagement is going well, that is usually her doing.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="founder">
          <h3>Dan Levy</h3>
          <p class="role">Co-founder, principal AI engineer</p>
          <p>
            Engineer, educator, founder, and technical leader with more than
            twenty-five years across production systems, developer platforms,
            AI applications, evaluation infrastructure, and offensive and
            defensive AI security. He grew one platform organization from six
            engineers to sixty and has shipped systems used by fifty million
            people. He still writes the code on every engagement.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="mailto:dan@danlevy.net">dan@danlevy.net</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container section-grid">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2>How we think</h2>
        <p>Three convictions that show up in every piece of work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principles">
        <div>
          <h3>Evidence over theater</h3>
          <p>
            A fluent demo is not a reliable system. We design measurement that
            survives scrutiny from your engineers, your customers, and your
            auditors.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Security is architecture</h3>
          <p>
            Permissions, boundaries, data flows, and failure recovery belong in
            the design. Bolting them on at launch is how agents end up in the
            news.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Capability has to transfer</h3>
          <p>
            The engagement pays off when your team leaves with sharper systems
            and stronger judgment, and does not need us for the next change.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Work with us.</h2>
      <p>Send the problem, not a pitch. We will tell you if we can help.</p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
